%main.site-main
  %section.section.hero
    .section__number 01
    .section__body
      %h1.hero__name
        Elle
        %br/
        Meredith
      %p.hero__tagline
        Executive consultant and leadership coach, with 20+ years in
        software engineering.
      .hero__meta
        %span!= 'Currently — <a class="link" href="http://blackmill.co">Blackmill</a>'
        %span!= 'Previously Director of Eng at thoughtbot and orderly meds'
        %span 20+ years in software

  %section.section.bio
    .section__number 02
    .section__body.bio__columns
      .bio__column
        %p Elle is a well-rounded executive consultant and leadership coach with a background in software engineering. Her strengths are asking difficult questions while focusing on the bigger picture and business goals, growing high performing teams and leaders, and communicating with all relevant stakeholders.
        %p Elle is passionate about creating an environment that brings out the best in people. While she is an accomplished technologist, she believes in balancing business results with people retention. She leads with curiosity, understanding the “why” gives her the context to lead with integrity.
        %p Elle developed and ran two six-month engineering academies for Qantas Hotels and Disco. The curriculum covered programming fundamentals, clean code, refactoring, and agile workflows. She was on the Victorian Government’s Industry Advisory Panel to help assess digital skills training courses for the new Digital Skills and Jobs Program.
      .bio__column
        %p In 2021, she completed a post-grad certificate in Psychology for Business and Management at Curtin University. In 2025, she started her Masters in Leadership and Management (organisation dynamics) with NIODA.
        %p She believes in writing clean code, driven by automatic tests, with agile practices, an even work/life balance, and a respectful and inclusive team culture. Her aim is to deliver clean, functional and user‑friendly applications in an appropriate timeframe without wasting resources.
        %p!= 'When she is not immersed in the Ruby community, she is probably immersed in water, or lately, <a class="link" href="https://www.instagram.com/ellebread/">in bread flour</a>.'

  %section.section.community
    .section__number 03
    .section__body
      %h2.section__label Community
      %p.community__text
        != 'Elle has a passion for helping people learn to work better. She appreciates the value of strong communities. In 2014, she organised <a class="link" href="http://railsgirls.com/sydney">Rails Girls events in Sydney</a>, <a class="link" href="http://www.rubyconf.org.au/2014">RubyConfAU 2014</a>, and was a member of the <a class="link" href="https://ruby.org.au/">Ruby Australia</a> committee. In 2015, she co-organised <a class="link" href="http://2015.goruco.com/">Gotham Ruby Conference (GORUCO)</a> in New York City, and started a monthly work jelly for women in tech. In 2016, she co-organised <a class="link" href="https://www.instagram.com/p/BEJevFdJHxt/">Rails Camp USA East Coast</a> in the Catskills, NY and once again co-organised <a class="link" href="http://2016.goruco.com/">GORUCO X</a>. In 2018, she helped with the last <a class="link" href="http://goruco.com/">GORUCO conference</a>.'

  %section.section.testimonials{tabindex: 0}
    .section__number 04
    .section__body
      %h2.section__label Testimonials
      .testimonials__viewport
        - testimonials.each_with_index do |testimonial, index|
          %blockquote.testimonials__quote{class: ("is-active" if index.zero?), data: { author: testimonial["author"] }}
            %p= testimonial["quote"]
      .testimonials__controls
        %cite.testimonials__cite= testimonials.first["author"]
        .testimonials__nav
          %span.testimonials__counter= "01 / %02d" % testimonials.length
          %button.testimonials__btn.testimonials__btn--prev{type: "button", "aria-label": "Previous testimonial"}!= '&larr;'
          %button.testimonials__btn.testimonials__btn--next{type: "button", "aria-label": "Next testimonial"}!= '&rarr;'

%section.values
  .container.section
    .section__number 05
    .section__body
      %h2.section__label Work values
      %ol.values__list
        %li
          %span.values__num 01
          Work with friends, or people who will become my friends
        %li
          %span.values__num 02
          Write clean code accompanied with tests
        %li
          %span.values__num 03
          A learning and growth mindset culture
        %li
          %span.values__num 04
          Values collaboration and people’s opinions
        %li
          %span.values__num 05
          Good work etiquette and respect for peers
        %li
          %span.values__num 06
          Maintains work‑life balance
        %li
          %span.values__num 07
          Flexible with remote work
        %li
          %span.values__num 08
          Autonomy and agency
        %li
          %span.values__num 09
          Good pay

%section.talks
  .container.section
    .section__number 06
    .section__body
      %h2.section__label Talks
      %ol.talks__list{data: { collapse: 8 }}
        - talks.each do |talk|
          %li.talks__item
            = talk["title"]
            %span.talks__venue= talk["venue"]
      %button.talks__toggle{type: "button", hidden: true}= "Show all #{talks.length} talks"
